From ddcf7a96e48615a9dd3f72a19b24b5b708aba89d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:34:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Workstream 09: bridge10 on workstream 10's one lot table
 (from 10)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A patch from workstream 10, answering CONNECT-10 §5.4 T1, T3 and T4.
The bridge no longer keeps lots used under a use order in a table of its
own: they are workstream 10's LotCustody lots, beside the user's own.

- deposit_from_lot: 10's release_by_order consumes once per (job,
  deposit) and leaves the ore in 10's transit place; 09's Deposit takes
  it from there. The replay record and the rollback are unchanged.
- The decided claim: the unused ore goes back through 10's
  try_return_unused, un-consumed (CONSUMED -= q, IN_TOTAL unchanged),
  instead of a return caravan that counted it as used and as received
  again. The sub-unit rest, and all of it while the lot is frozen or
  full, is owed in 10's custody (Bridge::owed and ::returned read it).
- Bridge::add_lot / lot / edit_lot / vault_mut replace the lots and
  vaults maps in the tests; save/load keep only 09's state, 10's custody
  inside it, and the links.
- Tests: the expectations that encoded the double count change (the
  random run: CONSUMED = taken - returned, IN_TOTAL never moves; the
  decided claim: CONSUMED 6, not 40, after 34 of 40 came back); one new
  test that own lots and lots used under an order are one table.
- run.sh pins workstream 10 at b237b581 (custody tree b91cbfdd,
  adapter-09 tree b8b5984c) and runs 10's adapter tests with
  nine-refused (10's reasons in CustodyError::Refused, T2).

Nothing here decides the mixed sources (MixedSource stays as 09 added
it) or adds a resource to lots.

